>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> yes, in <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.15.0">Traverse v0.15.0</a>. Discover → execute → trace, on one shared <code>runtime.wasm</code>. Kotlin <code>com.traverse-framework:traverse-embedder</code> 0.15.0 on Maven Central and .NET <code>TraverseEmbedder</code> 0.15.0 on nuget.org both include <code>ExactModelHost</code>. <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1651">#1651</a> is closed. The published 0.14.0 packages did not include it.</p>

  <h2>What a published consumer can run</h2>
  <p>Native Rust and <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.15.0</code> execute signed exact-ref. Swift <code>ExactModelHost</code> is on the <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/swift-host-v0.15.0"><code>swift-host-v0.15.0</code></a> xcframework, which <code>Package.swift</code> on main pins. Distribution is GitHub Release + SPM binary target, not a CocoaPods claim. Full matrix: <a href="/questions/which-hosts-run-signed-exact-ref-models.html">Which hosts run signed exact-ref models?</a>.</p>

  <h2>What shipped in the 0.15.0 packages</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Kotlin <code>ExactModelHost</code> runs on <code>wasmi</code> through the <code>traverse-android-host</code> JNI shim (<a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1580">#1580</a>). The 0.15.0 AAR is on Maven Central.</li>
    <li>.NET <code>ExactModelHost</code> runs through two audited P/Invoke functions (<a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1602">#1602</a>). nuget.org lists <code>TraverseEmbedder</code> 0.15.0. The package ships the native engine for <code>win-x64</code>, <code>win-arm64</code>, and <code>linux-x64</code>.</li>
    <li>Both hosts enforce <code>model_usage</code>. Omitting it fails closed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Honest consumers</h2>
  <p>Shipped consumers for capabilities today: JS/TS + Rust embedders + MCP; Python via CLI only. Swift, Kotlin, and .NET are published, pre-1.0, and not Certified under Spec 529. Check <a href="/platforms.html">Platforms</a> and <a href="/what-is-real-today.html">what is real today</a> before quoting. The v0.14.0 embedder notes stay historical: <a href="/blog/traverse-0-14-0-what-changed-for-embedders.html">v0.14.0: what changed for embedders</a>.</p>
</QuestionLayout>
